{"path":"container/flat_multimap/rbegin","title":"std::flat_multimap<Key,T,Compare,KeyContainer,MappedContainer>::rbegin, std::flat_multimap<Key,T,Compare,KeyContainer,MappedContainer>::crbegin","titleHtml":"<span class=\"t-title-prefix\">std::flat_multimap&lt;Key,T,Compare,KeyContainer,MappedContainer&gt;::</span>rbegin, <span class=\"t-title-prefix\">std::flat_multimap&lt;Key,T,Compare,KeyContainer,MappedContainer&gt;::</span>crbegin","originalUrl":"https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/container/flat_multimap/rbegin","section":"container","kind":"page","summary":"Returns a reverse iterator to the first element of the reversed flat_multimap. It corresponds to the last element of the non-reversed flat_multimap.","html":"<table class=\"t-dcl-begin\"><tbody>\n<tr class=\"t-dcl t-since-cxx23\" id=\"Version_1\">\n<td> <div><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\">reverse_iterator rbegin<span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span> <span class=\"kw1\">noexcept</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span></span></div></td>\n<td> (1) </td>\n<td> <span class=\"t-mark-rev t-since-cxx23\">(since C++23)</span> </td>\n</tr>\n<tr class=\"t-dcl t-since-cxx23\" id=\"Version_2\">\n<td> <div><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\">const_reverse_iterator rbegin<span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span> <span class=\"kw4\">const</span> <span class=\"kw1\">noexcept</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span></span></div></td>\n<td> (2) </td>\n<td> <span class=\"t-mark-rev t-since-cxx23\">(since C++23)</span> </td>\n</tr>\n<tr class=\"t-dcl t-since-cxx23\" id=\"Version_3\">\n<td> <div><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\">const_reverse_iterator crbegin<span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span> <span class=\"kw4\">const</span> <span class=\"kw1\">noexcept</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span></span></div></td>\n<td> (3) </td>\n<td> <span class=\"t-mark-rev t-since-cxx23\">(since C++23)</span> </td>\n</tr>\n<tr class=\"t-dcl-sep\"><td></td><td></td><td></td></tr>\n</tbody></table>\n<p>Returns a reverse iterator to the first element of the reversed <code>flat_multimap</code>. It corresponds to the last element of the non-reversed <code>flat_multimap</code>. If the <code>flat_multimap</code> is empty, the returned iterator is equal to <span class=\"t-lc\">rend()</span>.\n</p>\n<div class=\"t-image\">\n<p><img alt=\"range-rbegin-rend.svg\" src=\"/cppreference/images/3/39/range-rbegin-rend.svg\" width=\"589\" height=\"250\">\n</p>\n</div>\n<h3 id=\"Parameters\">Parameters</h3>\n<p>(none)\n</p>\n<h3 id=\"Return_value\">Return value</h3>\n<p>Reverse iterator to the first element.\n</p>\n<h3 id=\"Complexity\">Complexity</h3>\n<p>Constant.\n</p>\n<h3 id=\"Notes\">Notes</h3>\n<p>The <a href=\"/w/cpp/iterator/reverse_iterator/base\">underlying iterator</a> of the returned reverse iterator is the <a href=\"/w/cpp/container/flat_multimap/end\">end iterator</a>. Hence the returned iterator is invalidated if and when the end iterator is invalidated.</p>\n<h3 id=\"Example\">Example</h3>\n<div class=\"t-example\">\n<pre data-lang=\"cpp\"><code><span class=\"co2\">#include &lt;algorithm&gt;</span>\n<span class=\"co2\">#include &lt;iostream&gt;</span>\n<span class=\"co2\">#include &lt;string&gt;</span>\n<span class=\"co2\">#include &lt;flat_map&gt;</span>\n&nbsp;\n<span class=\"kw4\">int</span> main<span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span>\n<span class=\"br0\">{</span>\n    <a href=\"/w/cpp/container/flat_multimap\"><span class=\"kw3360\">std::<span class=\"me2\">flat_multimap</span></span></a><span class=\"sy1\">&lt;</span><a href=\"/w/cpp/string/basic_string\"><span class=\"kw1238\">std::<span class=\"me2\">string</span></span></a>, <span class=\"kw4\">int</span><span class=\"sy1\">&gt;</span> map\n    <span class=\"br0\">{</span>\n        <span class=\"br0\">{</span><span class=\"st0\">\"█\"</span>, <span class=\"nu0\">1</span><span class=\"br0\">}</span>,\n        <span class=\"br0\">{</span><span class=\"st0\">\"▒\"</span>, <span class=\"nu0\">5</span><span class=\"br0\">}</span>,\n        <span class=\"br0\">{</span><span class=\"st0\">\"░\"</span>, <span class=\"nu0\">3</span><span class=\"br0\">}</span>,\n        <span class=\"br0\">{</span><span class=\"st0\">\"▓\"</span>, <span class=\"nu0\">7</span><span class=\"br0\">}</span>,\n        <span class=\"br0\">{</span><span class=\"st0\">\"▓\"</span>, <span class=\"nu0\">8</span><span class=\"br0\">}</span>,\n        <span class=\"br0\">{</span><span class=\"st0\">\"░\"</span>, <span class=\"nu0\">4</span><span class=\"br0\">}</span>,\n        <span class=\"br0\">{</span><span class=\"st0\">\"▒\"</span>, <span class=\"nu0\">6</span><span class=\"br0\">}</span>,\n        <span class=\"br0\">{</span><span class=\"st0\">\"█\"</span>, <span class=\"nu0\">2</span><span class=\"br0\">}</span>\n    <span class=\"br0\">}</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span>\n&nbsp;\n    <a href=\"/w/cpp/io/cout\"><span class=\"kw1775\">std::<span class=\"me2\">cout</span></span></a> <span class=\"sy1\">&lt;&lt;</span> <span class=\"st0\">\"Print out in reverse order using const reverse iterators:<span class=\"es1\">\\n</span>\"</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span>\n    <a href=\"/w/cpp/algorithm/for_each\"><span class=\"kw1580\">std::<span class=\"me2\">for_each</span></span></a><span class=\"br0\">(</span>map.<span class=\"me1\">crbegin</span><span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span>, map.<span class=\"me1\">crend</span><span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span>,\n        <span class=\"br0\">[</span><span class=\"br0\">]</span><span class=\"br0\">(</span><a href=\"/w/cpp/utility/pair\"><span class=\"kw1104\">std::<span class=\"me2\">pair</span></span></a><span class=\"sy1\">&lt;</span><span class=\"kw4\">const</span> <a href=\"/w/cpp/string/basic_string\"><span class=\"kw1238\">std::<span class=\"me2\">string</span></span></a>, <span class=\"kw4\">int</span><span class=\"sy1\">&gt;</span> <span class=\"kw4\">const</span><span class=\"sy3\">&amp;</span> e<span class=\"br0\">)</span>\n        <span class=\"br0\">{</span>\n            <a href=\"/w/cpp/io/cout\"><span class=\"kw1775\">std::<span class=\"me2\">cout</span></span></a> <span class=\"sy1\">&lt;&lt;</span> <span class=\"st0\">\"{ <span class=\"es1\">\\\"</span>\"</span> <span class=\"sy1\">&lt;&lt;</span> e.<span class=\"me1\">first</span> <span class=\"sy1\">&lt;&lt;</span> <span class=\"st0\">\"<span class=\"es1\">\\\"</span>, \"</span> <span class=\"sy1\">&lt;&lt;</span> e.<span class=\"me1\">second</span> <span class=\"sy1\">&lt;&lt;</span> <span class=\"st0\">\" };<span class=\"es1\">\\n</span>\"</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span>\n        <span class=\"br0\">}</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span>\n&nbsp;\n    map.<span class=\"me1\">rbegin</span><span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span><span class=\"sy2\">-</span><span class=\"sy1\">&gt;</span>second <span class=\"sy1\">=</span> <span class=\"nu0\">42</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span> <span class=\"co1\">// OK: non-const value is modifiable</span>\n<span class=\"co1\">//  map.crbegin()-&gt;second = 42; // Error: cannot modify the const value</span>\n<span class=\"br0\">}</span></code></pre>\n<p>Possible output:\n</p>\n<pre data-output=\"1\"><code>Print out in reverse order using const reverse iterators:\n{ \"▓\", 8 };\n{ \"▓\", 7 };\n{ \"▒\", 6 };\n{ \"▒\", 5 };\n{ \"░\", 4 };\n{ \"░\", 3 };\n{ \"█\", 2 };\n{ \"█\", 1 };</code></pre> \n</div>\n<h3 id=\"See_also\">See also</h3>\n<table class=\"t-dsc-begin\">\n<tr class=\"t-dsc\">\n<td>  <div class=\"t-dsc-member-div\"><div><a href=\"/w/cpp/container/flat_multimap/rend\"> <span class=\"t-lines\"><span>rend</span><span>crend</span></span></a></div></div>\n</td>\n<td>  returns a reverse iterator to the end <br> <span class=\"t-mark\">(public member function)</span> </td></tr>\n<tr class=\"t-dsc\">\n<td>  <div class=\"t-dsc-member-div\"><div><a href=\"/w/cpp/iterator/rbegin\"> <span class=\"t-lines\"><span>rbegin</span><span>crbegin</span></span></a></div><div><span class=\"t-lines\"><span><span class=\"t-mark-rev t-since-cxx14\">(C++14)</span></span></span></div></div>\n</td>\n<td>  returns a reverse iterator to the beginning of a container or array <br> <span class=\"t-mark\">(function template)</span> </td></tr>\n</table>","headings":[{"depth":3,"text":"Parameters","id":"Parameters"},{"depth":3,"text":"Return value","id":"Return_value"},{"depth":3,"text":"Complexity","id":"Complexity"},{"depth":3,"text":"Notes","id":"Notes"},{"depth":3,"text":"Example","id":"Example"},{"depth":3,"text":"See also","id":"See_also"}],"breadcrumbs":[{"path":"","title":"C++ reference"},{"path":"container","title":"Containers library"},{"path":"container/flat_multimap","title":"std::flat_multimap"}],"children":[],"map":{"label":"std::flat_multimap<Key,T,Compare,KeyContainer,MappedContainer>::rbegin, std::flat_multimap<Key,T,Compare,KeyContainer,MappedContainer>::crbegin","children":[{"label":"Declarations","note":"3 declarations; revisions: since C++23. Returns a reverse iterator to the first element of the reversed flat_multimap."},{"label":"Parameters","note":"(none)"},{"label":"Return value","note":"Reverse iterator to the first element."},{"label":"Complexity","note":"Constant."},{"label":"Notes","note":"The underlying iterator of the returned reverse iterator is the end iterator."},{"label":"Example"},{"label":"See also","children":[{"label":"rend, crend","note":"returns a reverse iterator to the end"},{"label":"rbegin, crbegin","note":"returns a reverse iterator to the beginning of a container or array"}]}]},"standards":["C++14","C++23"],"wordCount":252,"codeBlockCount":2}
